{"name":"Lake Placid","hex":"#aeb9bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lake Placid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States:\nA small lake in Collier County, Florida. \nA town and lake in Highlands County, Florida. \nA village and lake in the town of North Elba, Essex County, New York. \nA reservoir in Guadalupe County, Texas.","A small lake in Collier County, Florida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lake_Placid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lake Placid, New York","blocks":[{"text":"Lake Placid is a village in Essex County, New York, United States, within the Adirondack Mountains. Its population was 2,205 at the 2020 census. Lake Placid became known internationally for hosting the 1932 and the 1980 Winter Olympics. Lake Placid has also hosted the 1972 and 2023 Winter World University Games, as well as the 2000 Goodwill Winter Games. The village is near the center of the town of North Elba, 50 miles (80 km) southwest of Plattsburgh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Lake_Placid_from_McKenzie_Mountain.jpg/330px-Lake_Placid_from_McKenzie_Mountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Placid%2C_New_York","wikidata":"Q192700"},{"title":"Lake Placid (New York)","blocks":[{"text":"The body of water named Lake Placid is located in the Adirondack Mountains in northern New York, United States. It is located on the northern side of the Village of Lake Placid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Lake_Placid.jpg/330px-Lake_Placid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Placid_(New_York)","wikidata":"Q1801051"},{"title":"Lake Placid (film series)","blocks":[{"text":"Lake Placid is a series of American comedy horror films created by David E. Kelley. The series began with Lake Placid (1999) directed by Steve Miner, and was followed by five television sequels, Lake Placid 2 (2007) by David Flores, Lake Placid 3 (2010) by Griff Furst, Lake Placid: The Final Chapter (2012) by Don Michael Paul, Lake Placid vs. Anaconda (2015) by A.B. Stone, being a crossover with the Anaconda film series, and Lake Placid: Legacy (2018) by Darrell Roodt, which acting as direct sequel to the 1999 film, ignoring the other four sequels. Each installment revolves around the presence of giant man-eating crocodiles in the fictional location of Black Lake, Maine, and the efforts of various groups to capture or destroy the creatures. All of the films reference members of the fictitious Bickerman family."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Lake_Placid_-_Collector%27s_Edition_Blu-ray_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Placid_(film_series)","wikidata":"Q107211019"},{"title":"Lake","blocks":[{"text":"A lake is often a naturally occurring, relatively large and fixed body of water on or near the Earth's surface. It is localized in a basin or interconnected basins surrounded by dry land. Lakes lie completely on land and are separate from the ocean, although they may be connected with the ocean by outflowing rivers. Lakes, like other bodies of water, are part of the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Most lakes are fresh water and account for almost all the world's surface freshwater, but some are salt lakes with salinities even higher than that of seawater. Lakes vary significantly in surface area and volume of water, but in total cover approximately 2.5 × 106 km2 (less than 2%) of the Earth's surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg/330px-Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake","wikidata":"Q23397"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-New_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lake Placid in 1936","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_York_-_Lake_Placid_-_NARA_-_68145104_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg/500px-Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg/1280px-Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg/500px-Ceremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Opening Ceremony of the 1980 Winter Olympics in Lake Placid.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeremony_1980_Winter_Games.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg/500px-Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg/1280px-Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg/500px-Olympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Works Progress Administration poster from the late 1930s to advertise public access to the Mt. Van Hoevenberg Olympic Bobsled Run","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOlympic_Bobsled_Run_Lake_Placid2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ironman_2006.jpg/500px-Ironman_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ironman_2006.jpg/1280px-Ironman_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ironman_2006.jpg/500px-Ironman_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"2006 Ironman in Lake Placid","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIronman_2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg/500px-North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg/1280px-North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg/500px-North_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Elba Showgrounds, showing Horse Rings, Olympic Cauldron, Whiteface Mountain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_Elba_Showgrounds.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi